  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Protection, Assistance, and Mental Health and Psychosocial Support (MHPSS) for Vulnerable Communities and Migrants at Risk of Human Trafficking or Other Types of Violence and Abuse</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will focus on the provision of emergency protection, assistance, and Mental Health and Psychosocial Support (MHPSS) for vulnerable communities and migrants at risk of human trafficking or other types of violence and abuse in the states of Bolivar, Falcon, Sucre and Zulia in Venezuela. Through this project, IOM aims at reaching a total of 14,549 people.&#xa0; The overarching objective of IOM&#x2019;s strategy is to prevent, mitigate and respond to immediate protection risks associated with irregular, unsafe and high-risk migration pathways through community-based emergency protection and MHPSS assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
